/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Functions: refocus, reread, client, mountStart, mountPage, withChanges, applied, routeStart, startButton,
 *              openStart, writesOf, openEditor, rangeBox, updateButton, routeSummary, notStarted,
 *              routePairingSave, saveDraft, readsOf, answeredIdentity, discardedJson, expectDiscardedPage
 *   Constants: summary, create, numberInputs, discardedNotice
 * Tests
 *   - creating a review confirms the frozen Album and only creates a private project whose free lookup the server starts, never Luna AI
 *   - where lookup is not configured, the action creates an Album completion for manual editing
 *   - an Album revision change leaves its open creation approval disabled instead of silently rebasing
 *   - an unconfirmed review creation retries the original UUID and snapshot only when explicitly requested
 *   - without catalog editing the Album page action stays disabled and says new completions are off, while an open completion is still linked
 *   - an open completion's note says what its lookup found, and the plain note stays when the server sends no brief
 *   - an open completion's note follows its active lookup until the lookup ends
 *   - a review page has no tabs or step bar, and the sticky action bar ends it with the update as its primary button, whose wait reason describes it
 *   - an open completion on an Album that cannot have another is linked, and Start another completion is disabled with the reason
 *   - the eligibility is read for the Album revision shown, and again for a newer revision
 *   - reopening and manual editing touch only the private review, preserving catalog projections and identity controls
 *   - Luna analysis requires its own confirmation and a lost acknowledgement never retries automatically
 *   - a durable unknown provider outcome prevents another paid generation while retaining manual review
 *   - Artist-only suggestions explain separate attribution management without offering identity adoption
 *   - a label suggestion is an identity hint beside the Artist hints that can only be kept, while a Disc Number suggestion is a Review item
 *   - a label-only review shows only its hint in the Luna AI suggestions section, reads a missing label as no value, and a kept hint offers nothing more
 *   - an Artist hint for an Album without Credits context reads the empty baseline and current values as no value
 *   - an applied historical review shows its outcome view, read-only, and never starts work when reopened
 *   - selected suggestion adoption and independent rejection preserve manual values and exclude Artist identity hints
 *   - with nothing to save, the update skips the save and confirms only the selected saved fields, then invalidates projections only after its receipt
 *   - going back from the confirmation keeps the saved draft, says the Album is unchanged and focuses the update again
 *   - a newer saved revision disables an open confirmation rather than rebasing its frozen selection
 *   - a review saved by a newer release refuses a save with a reload request and no retry
 *   - changing review routes cannot show or retry another project unknown intent
 *   - same-revision refresh keeps the update range's selection, but a newer saved value requires selecting it again
 *   - a delayed successful Save cannot overwrite a newer observed revision or erase its conflict when refresh fails
 *   - analysis progress never makes a local edit stale, while another administrator change does
 *   - completed review guidance is read-only and no longer invites draft editing or a paid run
 *   - the draft shows ordered Credits, join phrases and the label as read-only context and edits Disc Numbers only where captured
 *   - a review opened before Disc Numbers were captured shows no Disc Number input and offers no disc change
 *   - a v1 review response the strict schema refuses asks for a reload instead of showing a partial review
 *   - a captured review saves only changed editable values, never its expected tracklist or member Artist entries
 *   - each save is based on the draft the last save stored, so a second save sends the first saved value as its base
 *   - an edit changed back to the saved value leaves nothing to save
 *   - a save refused because another administrator changed the value reloads the saved review and offers it, which ends the refusal
 *   - the status line comes first and the lookup controls precede the paid Luna AI button, which is never primary, and Luna AI suggestions arrive unticked
 *   - the page follows the v3 order: the status line, the proposed changes, the update range, the lookup details, the row of alternatives, then Luna AI
 *   - Look up another name opens the name box under the row of alternatives, Cancel closes it and returns the focus, and it waits for unsaved edits only while closed
 *   - a failed Luna AI run is one quiet line under Other actions while the lookup asks for numbers, which the proposal table holds
 *   - an applied review shows no lookup summary and never reads it
 *   - on open the table proposes the numbers the captured titles give, selected; pending proposals hold neither lookup nor Luna AI, and a save sends only them
 *   - the update takes two clicks: it saves the selected proposals, confirms the frozen selection inline, focused on its back button, then applies it
 *   - a number typed over a proposal is an unsaved edit that holds lookup and Luna AI, and a proposal cleared or deselected is never saved
 *   - a member's own number is kept, so only the empty numbers are proposed, marked as filling, and saved
 *   - a stored number that disagrees with its title stops the proposal and names the track, so no two members can claim one position
 *   - lookup waits for unsaved draft edits, which the bar offers to save alone
 *   - a lookup submission, a choice and an answer are sent with the shown revision, and their receipts are read without a reload
 *   - a lookup refusal shows its own message and keeps no intent to retry
 *   - a lookup application at the same revision disables an open confirmation once the summary notices its value revision
 *   - identity decisions are saved with the shown revision as soon as one is chosen; a stale refusal reads the review, its summary and identity rows again, keeping the unsaved choice to send again
 *   - a member deselected in the update range stays deselected after an identity decision is saved, while the lists it answered arrive selected
 *   - a choice whose response was lost is offered again as the original operation with its operation ID, and lookup waits meanwhile
 *   - the free retry sends only the shown revision and its operation ID, and its receipt leads to a new summary read
 *   - an answer refused because the lookup changed shows its own message and reads the summary and identity rows again
 *   - an apply confirmed before the page saw a lookup application is refused as stale by its value revision, reads the review again and keeps nothing to retry
 *   - a number lookup filled through its pairing applies with its tracklist, and waits for it when the tracklist is deselected
 *   - a confirmation shows every selected change, member line and identity, and sends the identity items and members it showed
 *   - an apply refused because an identity needs an answer again returns to editing, reads the review, its summary and identity rows again and keeps nothing to retry
 *   - Discard completion ends the row of alternatives after manual editing and before the paid Luna AI action, is never primary, and is disabled with its reason while Luna AI runs
 *   - a review whose refreshed read is answered as discarded shows only the discarded notice with Back, without the action bar, and forgets its draft
 *   - a review with Luna AI running whose poll is answered as discarded is never read again, by its poll or on window focus
 *   - a review change answered as discarded shows only the discarded notice
 *   - a lookup summary read answered as discarded also ends the page
 *   - an unconfirmed creation retried after its completion was discarded says so, keeps nothing to retry and reads the eligibility again
 * @end-catalog */

import { act, cleanup, fireEvent, render, screen, waitFor, within } from '@testing-library/react';
